<title>UK: M&amp;S buoyed by store purchase, trading news.</title>
<headline>M&amp;S buoyed by store purchase, trading news.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-07-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Marks and Spencer Plc shares put on 5p to 592p in busy trading after news from the annual shareholders' meeting.</p>
<p>M&amp;S said first quarter clothing sales rose nearly 10 percent and food 2.3 percent. The retailer said it was buying 19 stores from Littlewoods for 192.5 million stg and that the acquisition would enhance shareholder value.</p>
<p>&quot;Quite good on clothing considering the difficult weather and poor on food in line with the recent trend,&quot; said one analyst.</p>
<p>&quot;What's really encouraging is that they've got a decent slug of Littlewoods' stores. There's good potential there. Overall the news is not crucial but positive,&quot; he said.</p>
<p>-- Louise Ireland, London Newsroom +44 171 542 8712</p>
